 "pdCallTexts": [
  {
   "deadId": "gen_1hil9m4",
   "entryDay": 17,
   "cause": "the wild",
   "lines": [
    "d17: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Hannah Guerrero is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d17: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d17: 🕯️ Hannah Guerrero is dead — the wild. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d17: What Hannah kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d17: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Haftom blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d17: 📖 LEARNED: The Forager’s Eye (Level 1). You walk slower and see more. Food was always there; now you notice it.",
    "d17: 📖 LEARNED: Food Preservation (Level 1). Salt, smoke, dry. The big three. Salt draws water out; bacteria can't live without it.",
    "d17: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d17: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Hannah Guerrero, 17 days. The mantle passes to Haftom Haile.",
    "d17: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Haftom Haile, 58 — a Mushroom grower. Their hands know different work now: Bloodhound.",
    "d17: The village's quarrel was with Hannah — and Hannah is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
    "d17: The fire knew Haftom — solid ground, earned at this fire."
   ]
  },
  {
   "deadId": "gen_4e0x0cr",
   "entryDay": 85,
   "cause": "the wild",
   "lines": [
    "d85: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Haftom Haile is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d85: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d85: HAFTOM — GONE. 3 open questions closed unanswered.",
    "d85: 🕯️ Haftom Haile is dead — the wild. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d85: What Haftom kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d85: \"Haftom's gone.\" Jovan looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Haftom.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d85: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Luis blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d85: 📖 LEARNED: Stone & Masonry (Level 1). Stack stone so it stands: batter the wall, heart it with rubble, cap it well.",
    "d85: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d85: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Haftom Haile, 85 days. The mantle passes to Luis Fernandez.",
    "d85: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Luis Fernandez, 46 — a mason. His hands know different work now: Iron Stomach, Green Whisper, Berserker Rage, Lucky Rock.",
    "d85: The village's quarrel was with Haftom — and Haftom is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
    "d85: At the grave, Abraham, Jovan, Ingrid and 1 more speak for Luis — \"Haftom trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d85: The fire knew Luis before the Codex did — his name already carried weight here."
   ]
  }
 ],
